            <ArticleTitle>[Primary study on mechanism of baicalin on the Th1/Th2 response in murine model of asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1407-10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="OBJECTIVE" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">To study the mechanism of baicalin on the cytokines of Th1/Th2 in murine model of asthma.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="METHODS" NlmCategory="METHODS">The murine model of asthma was induced by OVA. Different doses of baicalin were orally administered to the mice respectively. The spleen cells were cultured 3 days for the measurement of IFN-gamma, IL-4, IL-5 and IL-10 by ELISA. After 2 days of culture, the spleen cells were treated with Trizol for extraction of total RNA. The gene expressions of T-bet, GATA-3 and STAT-6 were analyzed by RT-PCR.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RESULTS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">The treatment with baicalin obviously decreased the production of IL-4 and IL-5 and the gene expression of GATA-3, STAT-6, but increased the production of IL-10.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="CONCLUSION" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">Baicalin may modulate the Th1/Th2 balance mainly by altering the gene expressions of GATA-3 and STAT-6 in vivo and increasing the production of IL-10.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
